.TH JITTER_RNG 4 2026-09-30 "jitterentropy x.y.z" "Kernel Interfaces Manual"
.\" groff re-enables hyphenation per paragraph unless HY is 0.
.nr HY 0
.nh
.SH NAME
jitter_rng \- Linux kernel module of the CPU Jitter Random Number Generator
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B modprobe jitter_rng
.RI [ parameter = value " ...]"
.PP
.I /dev/jitterentropy
.br
.I /proc/jitterentropy/
.PP
.B #include <jitterentropy_uapi.h>
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B jitter_rng
is the CPU Jitter Random Number Generator of
.BR jitterentropy (3)
built for the Linux kernel, 5.10 or later, from the unchanged library
sources. The C interface of the library is not exported; the module offers
the Jitter RNG through the interfaces below instead. Each is a build option
of the module and may be absent;
.I /proc/jitterentropy/interfaces/
says which were compiled in.
.SS Character device
Every
.BR open (2)
of
.I /dev/jitterentropy
allocates an entropy collector of its own with the
.B osr
and
.B flags
of the module, and
.BR close (2)
frees it.
.BR read (2)
delivers its output in any size and recovers from an intermittent health
test failure as
.BR jent_read_entropy_safe ()
of
.BR jent_read_entropy (3)
does, reallocating the collector. With
.B O_NONBLOCK
a read delivers at most 32 bytes and fails with
.B EAGAIN
rather than wait while the instance is busy, see
.BR ERRORS .
.SS Hardware random number generator
The module registers one collector as
.I jitterentropy
with the
.I hw_random
framework. Once it is the current device in
.IR /sys/class/misc/hw_random/rng_current ,
.I /dev/hwrng
reads from it.
.SS Kernel crypto API
The module registers the random number generator
.I jitter_rng
- or
.IR jitterentropy_rng ,
the name of the kernel's own copy, when it is built into the kernel in its
place. Each instantiation allocates a collector. User space reaches it
through
.B AF_ALG
sockets of type
.IR rng .
.SS Status in procfs
.I /proc/jitterentropy/
holds the version, the effective configuration, the interfaces compiled in,
statistics, and the status document of
.BR jent_status (3)
for the hardware random number generator instance and for every open
character device instance; see
.BR FILES .
.SS Cryptographic self test
The known answer tests of
.BR jent_selftest ()
of
.BR jent_entropy_init (3)
run at module load, as part of the library's initialization, and for every
instance periodically if
.B selftest_interval
is set, or on demand with
.BR JENT_IOCSELFTEST .
An instance whose run fails stops delivering for good; a kernel booted with
.I fips=1
panics instead.
.SS Test interface
Off by default and not meant for production: the debugfs file
.IR /sys/kernel/debug/jitter_rng/jent_raw_hires ,
readable by root, delivers the raw time deltas of the noise source as 64 bit
values. Every open allocates a collector with
.B testing_osr
and
.BR testing_flags ,
without the startup, so that the configuration recorded is the one asked
for. The file is not created on a kernel without debugfs or on a
locked-down kernel.
.B getrawentropy
of the source distribution records from it.
.SH PARAMETERS
All but
.B testing_osr
and
.B testing_flags
are set at load time only.
.TP
.BR osr =\fIn\fR
The oversampling rate of every collector. 0, the default, and any value
below 3 select 3; a value above 20 refuses the load.
.TP
.BR flags =\fIn\fR
The
.B JENT_*
flags of every collector, as in
.BR jent_entropy_collector_alloc (3),
0 by default.
.B JENT_FORCE_INTERNAL_TIMER
- the module has no internal timer - and, in FIPS or NTG.1 mode,
.B JENT_DISABLE_MEMORY_ACCESS
refuse the load. The memory size and hash loop fields set the memory access
region and the hash loop count of every collector.
.TP
.BR ntg1 =1
AIS 20/31 NTG.1 compliant operation; sets
.BR JENT_NTG1 .
.TP
.BR force_fips =1
FIPS compliant operation; sets
.BR JENT_FORCE_FIPS .
A kernel booted with
.I fips=1
implies it.
.TP
.BR cache_all =1
Size the memory access region from all data caches; sets
.BR JENT_CACHE_ALL .
.TP
.BR selftest_interval =\fIn\fR
Seconds between two self test runs of each instance. 0, the default, runs
none after the load. A value above 2592000, 30 days, is lowered to it with a
warning.
.TP
.BR hwrng_quality =\fIn\fR
The entropy declared to
.IR hw_random ,
in bits per 1024 bits of output, 0 by default. A value above 1024 is lowered
to it with a warning. See
.BR NOTES .
.TP
.BR verbose =\fIn\fR
Not 0: log the status document of each crypto API instance when it is
created or reallocated, rate-limited, and of the test interface's instance
on an open whose
.B testing_osr
or
.B testing_flags
differ from the last one logged, as well as each passed self test.
.TP
.BR testing_osr =\fIn\fR ", " testing_flags =\fIn\fR
The oversampling rate and flags of the test interface, writable by root in
.I /sys/module/jitter_rng/parameters/
and read on every open. In
.BR testing_flags ,
bit 15 selects the NTG.1 hash loop and bit 16 the NTG.1 memory access loop
as the noise source to record; the hash loop wins when both are set.
.SH IOCTLS
Defined in
.IR jitterentropy_uapi.h .
The character device and the test interface implement them, on the instance
of the open file description, except where noted.
.TP
.B JENT_IOCSTATUS
Copy the status document into the buffer of a
.IR "struct jent_status_ioctl" .
A buffer too small fails with
.B EOVERFLOW
and reports the length needed.
.TP
.BR JENT_IOCUUID ", " JENT_IOCVERSION ", " JENT_IOCOSR ", " JENT_IOCFLAGS ", " JENT_IOCHEALTH ", " JENT_IOCOUTPUT ", " JENT_IOCREINIT
A single value of the status document: the identifier, the library version,
the oversampling rate, the flags, the health test failures, the output
counters and the reinitializations - what the
.B jent_entropy_collector_*
accessors of
.BR jent_status (3)
report in user space. The test interface's collector skips the startup that
assigns the identifier, so
.B JENT_IOCUUID
fails there with
.BR ENODATA .
.TP
.B JENT_IOCSELFTEST
Run the cryptographic self test. Requires
.BR CAP_SYS_ADMIN .
On the character device the run is that of the instance; on the test
interface it is bound to no instance and only reports the verdict.
.TP
.B JENT_IOCLOOPCNT
Test interface only, the character device fails it with
.BR ENOTTY :
set the loop count of the measurements recorded, a
.I __u64
up to 4294967295; 0, the default, keeps the configured one.
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B EAGAIN
A nonblocking read found the instance busy: another reader, its periodic self
test, or a status ioctl or
.I /proc
read of it. On every interface also a read whose intermittent health test
failure could not be recovered from.
.TP
.B EFAULT
The module load: the startup of the Jitter RNG failed - its self tests, the
timer, the startup health tests or the
.B osr
and
.B flags
it refuses; the kernel log names the error code. Under
.I fips=1
the kernel panics instead. A failed
.BR JENT_IOCSELFTEST .
On every interface a read on an instance with a permanent health test or
self test failure; under
.I fips=1
a permanent health test failure panics the kernel.
.TP
.B EINVAL
On the test interface: an open with a
.B testing_osr
above 20 or that records the memory access loop with
.BR JENT_DISABLE_MEMORY_ACCESS ,
a read of a size that is not a multiple of 8, and a
.B JENT_IOCLOOPCNT
above 4294967295.
.TP
.B EIO
A
.B JENT_IOCSTATUS
or a status file read for which no status document could be produced; an
open of the test interface whose self test of the conditioning failed.
.TP
.B ENODATA
A single value ioctl on an instance that has none.
.TP
.B ENOMEM
No memory for a collector, or its allocation was refused, as on a failure
of its startup health tests.
.TP
.B ENOTTY
An ioctl the file does not implement.
.TP
.B EOVERFLOW
A
.B JENT_IOCSTATUS
buffer too small for the status document.
.TP
.B EPERM
.B JENT_IOCSELFTEST
without
.BR CAP_SYS_ADMIN ;
an open of the test interface on a kernel locked down after the load.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /dev/jitterentropy
The character device.
.TP
.I /dev/hwrng
The output of the current hardware random number generator.
.TP
.I /proc/jitterentropy/version
The library version.
.TP
.I /proc/jitterentropy/config/
.IR flags ,
.IR flags_raw ,
.IR osr ,
.I ntg1
and
.IR fips :
the configuration in effect.
.I fips
reads 1 also for NTG.1 mode and on a kernel booted with
.IR fips=1 .
.TP
.I /proc/jitterentropy/interfaces/
.IR kcapi ,
.IR hwrng ,
.I chardev
and
.IR testing :
1 for an interface compiled in.
.TP
.I /proc/jitterentropy/statistics
The open and the cumulative character device instances and the self test
interval, runs and failures, as JSON.
.TP
.I /proc/jitterentropy/hwrng_status
The status document of the hardware random number generator instance.
.TP
.I /proc/jitterentropy/instances/
The status document of every open character device instance, named by its
UUID.
.TP
.I /sys/module/jitter_rng/parameters/
The parameters above.
.TP
.I /sys/kernel/debug/jitter_rng/jent_raw_hires
The test interface.
.SH NOTES
On Linux 6.2 and later the
.I hw_random
core promotes a
.B hwrng_quality
of 0 to its own default of 1024: the Jitter RNG is then credited with full
entropy, feeds the kernel random pool, and is preferred over a hardware
device declaring less. To keep it from being credited, set
.I rng_core.default_quality=0
on the kernel command line.
.PP
Building, DKMS, the build into the kernel and the details of every interface
are described in
.I linux_kernel/README.md
of the source distribution.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR jent_entropy_collector_alloc (3),
.BR jent_entropy_init (3),
.BR jent_read_entropy (3),
.BR jent_status (3),
.BR jitterentropy (3),
.BR random (4),
.BR modprobe (8)
